    "TweetText": "Jeff Dean explaining Google built a ChatGPT-style chatbot roughly a year before OpenAI released theirs.\n\nTens of thousands of Google employees were already using it and loved it.\n\nLeadership still killed any public launch because:\n\n• “What if people stop searching on Google?”\n• “What if it says inaccurate or ‘bad’ things?”\n\nGoogle invented the Transformer architecture, and still threw away the first-mover advantage for nothing.\n\nInnovator's Dilemma at its finest.",
    "Tweet Url": "https://x.com/linasbeliunas/status/2085256408543445043",
    "TweetCreatedDate": "2026-08-06T06:47:24.000Z",
    "MediaType": "video",
    "MediaImageUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2085255836729774080/img/eH0uHvgdN2CIpB2G.jpg",
    "MediaVideoUrl": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2085255836729774080/vid/avc1/640x360/h6mNFG3s4CPpANB1.mp4?tag=29",
    "HasLink": "True",
    "Translation": "",
